Program Bug_2_25_StartblockNestedUndetected;
// Bug 2.25: `@startblock` doesn't detect a missing or nested `@endblock`.
// The `@startblock` handler has an explicit check for "a block is
// already open" (`if (Node::m_staticBlockInfo.m_blockID != -1) { ... }`),
// but the error call inside it is commented out, so the check exists but
// currently does nothing: the active block state is just silently
// overwritten with the new one. This is asymmetric with the reverse
// mistake (an `@endblock` with no matching `@startblock` open), which
// DOES fail with a clear "Cannot end a block that hasn't been started."
// error.
//
// Method B (compile-time), no VICE step, and an INVERTED expectation from
// every other snippet in this batch: this is a missing-error bug, not a
// spurious one. Pre-fix expected behavior: this file compiles CLEAN (exit
// 0, .prg produced), even though BlockA is left open when BlockB starts -
// confirmed live, no error or warning of any kind is emitted. Post-fix,
// once the commented-out error is re-enabled, this exact file should FAIL
// to compile with a "block already started" style error instead - i.e.
// the pass/fail sense of "does this compile" flips at fix time, unlike
// every other Method B snippet in this batch where clean compilation is
// the fixed-and-working state.

@startblock $f000 "BlockA"
var
	a : byte = 0;

@startblock $f100 "BlockB"
var
	b : byte = 0;

@endblock

begin
	a := 1;
	b := 2;
	loop();
end.
